---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Documentation"
  description="Install, connect, and operate Veasel Code — local-first coding agent with approvals, providers, skills, and a loopback API."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE</p>
    <h1>
      Adopt Veasel in
      <br />
      <em>a few clear steps.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Everything you need to evaluate or run the current preview: install,
      connect a model, review work, and understand what stays local.
    </p>

    <nav class="guide-grid" aria-label="Documentation paths">
      <a
        class="guide-card guide-card-featured"
        href={`${basePath}/docs/install/`}
      >
        <span class="guide-card-mark">01</span>
        <h2>Install</h2>
        <p>Archives, Homebrew, AUR, or build from source.</p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Install <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/quickstart/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">02</span>
        <h2>First session</h2>
        <p>
          <code>/connect</code>, open a workspace, review a patch or command.
        </p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/tui/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">03</span>
        <h2>Terminal UI</h2>
        <p>Themes, slash commands, usage, and keyboard flow.</p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          TUI <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/providers/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">◌</span>
        <h2>Providers</h2>
        <p>OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic, Gemini, Meta, and locals.</p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Providers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/skills/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">✳</span>
        <h2>Skills & plugins</h2>
        <p>Discover SKILL.md roots and experimental Agent Plugins.</p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Skills <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">⌘</span>
        <h2>MCP servers</h2>
        <p>
          <code>/mcp add</code>, user/project scope, <code>.mcp.json</code>{" "}
          import, trust, and per-call approval.
        </p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          MCP <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/sessions/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">☷</span>
        <h2>Sessions & context</h2>
        <p>SQLite history, repository map, compaction, async turns.</p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Sessions <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/api/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">⇄</span>
        <h2>API & headless</h2>
        <p>
          Loopback HTTP, SSE, and <code>veasel run</code>.
        </p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          API <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/security/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">⌂</span>
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>Approvals, sandboxes by platform, and data flow.</p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Security <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/troubleshooting/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">?</span>
        <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
        <p>Connect, sandbox, and uncertain-turn recovery.</p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Fix it <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
    </nav>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Five-minute path</h2>
      <pre><code>veasel
# In the TUI:
/connect          # paste key → pick model
# open a workspace session, then ask a question
/patches          # when an edit is proposed
/commands         # when a shell proposal appears</code></pre>
      <p>
        Default API: <code>127.0.0.1:4097</code>. For API-only:{" "}
        <code>veasel serve</code>. Headless:{" "}
        <code>veasel run --prompt "…" --workspace . --json</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>What ships today (honest)</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>Loopback V server, SQLite sessions, OpenTUI client with themes</li>
        <li>
          Multi-provider chat, bounded workspace tools, review-gated edits /
          shell / MCP
        </li>
        <li>
          Skills discovery, repository map, adaptive compaction, durable async
          turns
        </li>
        <li>
          Platform shell sandboxes when backends are available (not Codex-level)
        </li>
        <li>
          Configured MCP add/manage (user + project scope, portable{" "}
          <code>.mcp.json</code> import, <code>/v1/mcp-servers</code>) plus
          experimental Agent Plugins — see the{" "}
          <a href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>MCP guide</a> and{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/compatibility/agent-plugins.md">
            compatibility ledger
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <aside class="callout">
      <strong>Deep contracts.</strong> OpenAPI, provider catalog, shell risk
      model, and threat model live in the{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/tree/main/docs">
        veasel repository docs
      </a>
      . This site summarizes what you need to adopt; it does not invent APIs.
    </aside>

    <p class="callout mascot-terms">
      <strong>Mascot artwork</strong> Veasel is the V language mascot. Pixel-art
      adaptations credit V contributors under{" "}
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/">CC BY-NC 4.0</a>
      . Commercial use needs separate permission.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
